{"id": "xiran", "name": "Hyrcanian Forests", "short": "Hyrcanian Forests", "place": "Iran", "lat": 36.7, "lon": 53.5, "side": "r", "cont": "Asia", "country": "Iran", "kind": "Forest", "park": true, "blurb": "Ancient beech forests on the wet Caspian slopes of the Alborz, ruled by the Persian leopard.", "tip": {"id": "leopard", "title": "Remove the Persian leopard", "text": "The leopard hunts roe deer, red deer and wild boar. Set Persian leopard to -100% and watch the deer and boar, then the young trees and plants they browse."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Hyrcanian forests", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyrcanian_forests"}, {"title": "UNESCO World Heritage: Hyrcanian Forests", "url": "https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1584/"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Persian leopard", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persian_leopard"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Caspian red deer", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caspian_red_deer"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Oriental beech", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oriental_beech"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Hyrcanian forests", "icon": "aspen", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.15, "desc": "Light reaching the forest floor limits growth beneath the dense summer canopy, so many understory plants rely on gaps and clearings."}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "caspian moisture and rain", "xh": 0.5}, {"id": "soil", "sp": "forest soil and leaf litter", "xh": 0.8, "desc": "Fallen leaves and wood build a damp organic soil that holds water and nutrients for the trees."}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.95, "desc": "Break down leaf litter, dead wood and carcasses, returning nutrients to the soil."}, {"id": "beech", "sp": "fagus orientalis", "xh": 0.12, "wiki": "Oriental beech", "desc": "The dominant tree of the Hyrcanian forest, especially in the middle mountain zone, and a source of beechnuts in autumn."}, {"id": "oak", "sp": "quercus castaneifolia", "xh": 0.3, "desc": "A common broad-leaved tree of the lower forest, producing acorns eaten by many animals."}, {"id": "hornbeam", "sp": "carpinus betulus", "xh": 0.5, "name": "European hornbeam", "desc": "A widespread broad-leaved tree of the Hyrcanian forests, often growing with beech and oak."}, {"id": "bracken", "sp": "pteridium aquilinum", "xh": 0.7, "desc": "A fern of forest clearings and edges that spreads across open ground.", "ic": "sage"}, {"id": "grass", "sp": "avena", "xh": 0.88}, {"id": "vole", "sp": "microtus socialis", "xh": 0.1}, {"id": "tit", "sp": "parus major", "xh": 0.28, "desc": "A small woodland bird that eats insects and, in autumn and winter, seeds such as beechnuts."}, {"id": "roe", "sp": "capreolus capreolus", "xh": 0.46, "desc": "A small deer that browses leaves, buds and herbs at forest edges and in clearings."}, {"id": "boar", "sp": "sus scrofa", "xh": 0.64, "desc": "An omnivore that roots in the forest floor for nuts, roots, plants and small animals."}, {"id": "reddeer", "sp": "cervus elaphus maral", "xh": 0.84}, {"id": "marten", "sp": "martes martes", "xh": 0.12, "desc": "A forest-dwelling hunter of small mammals and birds, recorded near the Hyrcanian forests.", "ic": "fox"}, {"id": "wildcat", "sp": "felis silvestris", "xh": 0.3, "name": "Wildcat", "desc": "A small forest cat that hunts rodents, birds and reptiles."}, {"id": "buzzard", "sp": "buteo buteo", "xh": 0.5, "desc": "The most recorded raptor in the area. It hunts voles and other small prey from perches and in flight."}, {"id": "jackal", "sp": "canis aureus", "xh": 0.7, "desc": "An opportunist that hunts small animals and also scavenges carcasses."}, {"id": "raven", "sp": "corvus corax", "xh": 0.9, "desc": "A scavenging crow that feeds on carrion and other food."}, {"id